# =============================================================================
# Config: HPRC v2 MC chm13 chr6 — HG002 noisy reads query (L=25)
# =============================================================================
# Query config for running find_mems + gafpack against the hprcv2-mc-chr6
# index using noisy HG002 reads.
#
# HG002 is IN-GRAPH for this index (present as HG002#1#chr6#... / HG002#2#chr6#...,
# 6 paths), unlike chr6.alt_noisy.reads.txt whose source contig
# (HG00438#2#JAHBCA010000010.1, an HPRCv1 assembly) is absent here — HPRCv2 MC
# carries a different assembly of HG00438 (CM089172.1 / CM089191.1). So this
# config is the genuinely in-graph workload for this graph; alt-reads is
# "same sample, different assembly". See configs/README.md.
#
# Usage:
#   ./query.sh hprcv2-mc-chr6-hg002-noisy-L25.env hprcv2-mc-chr6-2026-06-07 [query-name] [--gaf]
# =============================================================================

# ---- Inputs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# GBZ not needed at query time — included for provenance.
GBZ="$MEM_PROJ/hprcv2-mc/chr6/chr6.gbz"

# Reads file: 100K noisy reads from HG002, 200bp
READS="$MEM_PROJ/hprcv1/chr6.hg002_noisy.reads.txt"

# ---- Naming ---------------------------------------------------------------
# BASE must match the index files in runs/hprcv2-mc-chr6-2026-06-07/
BASE="hprcv2-mc-chm13-chr6"

# ---- Pipeline parameters --------------------------------------------------
MEM_LEN=25
MIN_OCC=1
VALIDATE_SAMPLE=2000

# ---- Not used at query time -----------------------------------------------
KMER=31
THREADS=16

# ---- Reference run for compare.sh (optional) ------------------------------
REF_DIR=""
REF_BASE=""
